# Enforce LF line endings for every text file in this repository.
#
# Root cause of the prior agent loop: Git (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) and
# Docker/CVS-style volume mounts convert CRLF <-> LF on checkout/commit, so the
# working tree carries CRLF, the index carries LF, and any diff surface shows a
# whitespace-only churn that agents keep "fixing" endlessly.
#
# With this file + `core.autocrlf = input`, Git stores and checks out LF
# everywhere, so the same bytes are on disk as in the repository and diffs are
# always about real content. SketchUp, Ruby, JSON and Markdown all read LF
# fine.
#
# References:
#   - https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes
#   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/ide/editor/configuration-options-for-line-endings

# Auto-detect text files; never treat unknown extensions as text.
* text=auto

# Source files must be committed and checked out as LF.
*.rb text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.markdown text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.erb text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.erb text eol=lf
*.sublime-build text eol=lf
*.rspec text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be converted (they are not tracked text).
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.tiff binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.exe binary
*.jar binary
*.skp binary
*.skb binary
*.layout binary
*.rbz binary
*.tx binary
